w when you're safe to ship.\nreferences/CodexBar/docs/index.html:91:            <li>One status item per provider (Codex, Claude, Cursor, Gemini, Antigravity, Droid, Copilot, z.ai).</li>\nreferences/CodexBar/docs/index.html:99:          <img src=\"./codexbar.png\" alt=\"CodexBar menu bar popover showing session and weekly usage.\" />\nreferences/CodexBar/docs/FORK_ROADMAP.md:148:   - Account dropdown in menu bar\nreferences/CodexBar/docs/FORK_ROADMAP.md:156:4. Add account switcher to menu bar\nreferences/CodexBar/docs/FORK_ROADMAP.md:214:- < 1 second menu bar response time\nreferences/CodexBar/docs/cli.md:6:  - \"Aligning menubar and CLI output/behavior.\"\nreferences/CodexBar/docs/cli.md:11:A lightweight Commander-based CLI that mirrors the menubar app’s data paths (Codex web/RPC → PTY fallback; Claude web by default with CLI fallback and OAuth debug).\nreferences/CodexBar/docs/cli.md:188:- Future: optional `--from-cache` flag to read the menubar app’s persisted snapshot (if/when that file lands).\nreferences/CodexBar/docs/ui.md:11:- LSUIElement app: no Dock icon; status item uses custom NSImage.\nreferences/CodexBar/docs/ui.md:12:- Merge Icons toggle combines providers into one status item with a switcher.\nreferences/CodexBar/docs/ui.md:19:- Advanced: menu bar can show provider branding icons with a percent label instead of critter bars.\nreferences/CodexBar/docs/session-keepalive-design.md:227:3. **Should we show keepalive status in menu bar?**\nreferences/CodexBar/docs/session-keepalive-design.md:230:   - **Recommendation:** Show in Settings only, not menu bar\nreferences/CodexBar/docs/RELEASING.md:101:- [ ] Release pages: title format `CodexBar <version>`, notes as Markdown list (no stray blank lines)\nreferences/CodexBar/docs/augment.md:46:1. Check the menu bar for the Augment icon\nreferences/CodexBar/appcast.xml:104:<li>Preferences: add per-provider menu bar metric picker (#185) — thanks @HaukeSchnau</li>\nreferences/CodexBar/appcast.xml:119:<li>Menu bar: re