{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_119","type":"reasoning","text":"**Planning window hide via explicit quit mode**\n\nTo hide the main window while keeping the app running, I'll set QuitMode::Explicit so closing the window doesn't quit the app, then recreate the window on demand from the tray menu. On macOS, the tray icon must be created after the event loop starts on the main thread, so I'll implement tray setup inside the app.run callback."}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_120","type":"reasoning","text":"**Designing cross-platform tray icon behavior**\n\nI'll create the tray icon after the event loop starts and store its state globally to keep it alive. For macOS, I'll keep menu shown on left click with an \"Open\" action, while on Windows I'll disable left-click menu to toggle the main window directly via click events, handling tray menu accordingly for both platforms."}}
